     ssnndd__eennvvyy2244 — VIA Envy24 and compatible bridge device driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ssoouunndd
           ddeevviiccee ssnndd__eennvvyy2244
           ddeevviiccee ssnndd__ssppiiccddss

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           snd_envy24_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssnndd__eennvvyy2244 bridge driver allows the generic audio driver sound(4) to
     attach to VIA Envy24 (ICE1724 or VT1724 chipset) and compatible audio de‐
     vices.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The ssnndd__eennvvyy2244 driver supports the following audio devices:

     ••   M-Audio Audiophile 2496
     ••   M-Audio Delta Dio 2496
     ••   Terratec DMX 6fire
     Only analog playback is supported.  Recording and other features of these
     cards are not supported.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     sound(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ssnndd__eennvvyy2244 device driver first appeared in FreeBSD 6.3.

